.\" pymnifocus-server man page
.TH PYMNIFOCUS\-SERVER 1 "July 2026" "pymnifocus 0.1.1" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
pymnifocus\-server \- MCP server for OmniFocus integration with AI assistants
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B pymnifocus\-server
.RI [ OPTIONS ]
.br
.B python \-m pymnifocus
.RI [ OPTIONS ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B pymnifocus\-server
runs a Model Context Protocol (MCP) server that enables AI assistants
such as Cursor, Claude Desktop, and Google Gemini to interact with
OmniFocus on macOS through natural language.
.PP
The server uses
.B stdio
transport by default and communicates with OmniFocus locally via OmniJS
scripts executed through
.BR osascript (1)
and AppleScript for write operations.
.PP
OmniFocus must be running for the server to function.
When using stdio transport, no network traffic leaves the machine.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BI \-\-transport " TRANSPORT"
Transport protocol to use:
.B stdio
(default) for local AI assistant integration, or
.B streamable\-http
for HTTP\-based clients and container access.
.TP
.BI \-\-host " HOST"
Bind address for HTTP transport.
Default:
.BR 127.0.0.1 .
Only used when transport is
.BR streamable\-http .
.TP
.BI \-\-port " PORT"
Port for HTTP transport.
Default:
.BR 8000 .
Only used when transport is
.BR streamable\-http .
.TP
.B \-h ", " \-\-help
Show usage information and exit.
.SH MCP TOOLS
The server exposes the following tools to connected AI clients:
.TP
.B query_omnifocus
Query tasks, projects, or folders with filters, sorting, and field selection.
.TP
.B dump_database
Get the complete current state of the OmniFocus database.
.TP
.B add_omnifocus_task
Add a new task with optional project, tags, due date, and other properties.
.TP
.B add_project
Create a new project with optional folder, tags, and configuration.
.TP
.B remove_item
Remove a task or project by ID or name.
.TP
.B edit_item
Edit properties of a task or project.
.TP
.B batch_add_items
Add multiple tasks or projects in a single operation (max 100).
.TP
.B batch_remove_items
Remove multiple tasks or projects in a single operation (max 100).
.TP
.B list_perspectives
List available OmniFocus perspectives.
.TP
.B get_perspective_view
Get items visible in a specific perspective.
.TP
.B list_tags
List all tags with hierarchy.
.SH MCP RESOURCES
The server provides the following read\-only resources:
.TP
.B omnifocus://inbox
Current inbox items.
.TP
.B omnifocus://today
Today's agenda: tasks due today, planned today, and overdue.
.TP
.B omnifocus://flagged
All flagged items.
.TP
.B omnifocus://stats
Database statistics (task, project, folder, and tag counts).
.TP
.B omnifocus://project/{name}
Tasks in a specific project.
.TP
.B omnifocus://perspective/{name}
Items in a named perspective.
.SH CONFIGURATION
.SS "Cursor"
Edit
.I ~/.cursor/mcp.json
to add:
.PP
.nf
.RS
{
  "mcpServers": {
    "omnifocus": {
      "command": "pymnifocus\-server"
    }
  }
}
.RE
.fi
.PP
Then restart Cursor or reload MCP servers.
.SS "Claude Desktop"
Edit
.IR "~/Library/Application Support/Claude/claude_desktop_config.json" :
.PP
.nf
.RS
{
  "mcpServers": {
    "omnifocus": {
      "command": "pymnifocus\-server"
    }
  }
}
.RE
.fi
.PP
Then restart Claude Desktop.
.SS "Streamable HTTP Transport"
For web\-based MCP clients or container access:
.PP
.nf
.RS
pymnifocus\-server \-\-transport streamable\-http
pymnifocus\-server \-\-transport streamable\-http \-\-port 9000
.RE
.fi
.PP
Then connect to
.IR http://localhost:8000/mcp
(or the configured port).
.SS "Container Access"
Since OmniFocus requires macOS, the server must run on the host.
Containers can reach it via
.B host.docker.internal
(Docker and Podman on macOS):
.PP
.nf
.RS
# On the macOS host:
pymnifocus\-server \-\-transport streamable\-http

# In the container's MCP config, connect to:
#   http://host.docker.internal:8000/mcp
.RE
.fi
.SH SECURITY
.IP \(bu 2
All user input is validated and escaped before embedding in scripts.
.IP \(bu 2
Entity names, sort fields, and field names are whitelisted.
.IP \(bu 2
Numeric parameters are validated as integers.
.IP \(bu 2
AppleScript strings are sanitized against injection.
.IP \(bu 2
Script paths are constrained to prevent directory traversal.
.IP \(bu 2
Batch operations are capped at 100 items.
.IP \(bu 2
Query results are capped at 5000 items.
.IP \(bu 2
All communication is local (no network traffic).
.SH ENVIRONMENT
Requires macOS with OmniFocus installed and running.
.SH EXIT STATUS
.TP
.B 0
Server shut down cleanly.
.TP
.B 1
Startup failure (e.g.\& missing dependencies).
